  "what_to_watch": [],
  "linkedin_post": "Institutional Bitcoin adoption is no longer about 'dipping a toe' in the water. Capital B's authorization to raise up to $120B for BTC acquisitions marks a pivot toward aggressive, large-scale corporate treasury strategies. When the scale of financing reaches this magnitude, it fundamentally changes the liquidity profile of the asset.\n\nSimultaneously, we see the 'infrastructure pivot' continuing, with mining firms like HIVE securing $220M AI contracts, and the rise of specialized compliance tools like Range. The trend is clear: the industry is maturing from speculative experimentation to institutional-grade financial architecture.\n\nAs corporate treasuries move from millions to billions, will we see a new wave of 'Bitcoin-backed' credit instruments become the standard for corporate finance?\n\n#Web3 #Bitcoin #VentureCapital #InstitutionalAdoption"
}